Consider the following classes:
```java
class Parent {
    void greet() { System.out.println("Hello from Parent"); }
}

class Child extends Parent {
    @Override
    void greet() { System.out.println("Hello from Child"); }
    void exclusive() { System.out.println("Child only"); }
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Parent p = new Child();
        p.greet();
    }
}
```
Which statement about the variable `p` is true?

Consider the following class:

```java
class Config {
    int maxRetries;
    boolean debug;
    String name;
}
```
If an instance of Config is created with `new Config()`, which statement about the values of its fields is correct?

Consider the following class:

class Widget {
