    default boolean equals(Object obj) {
        return true;
    }
}
```

Consider the following class:

class Example {
    int value;
    Example(int value) {
        this.value = value;
    }
}

Will the Java compiler automatically provide a no-argument default constructor for this class?

What does the following program print?

```java
class Animal {}
class Dog extends Animal {}
class Cat extends Animal {}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Animal a = new Cat();
        try {
            Dog d = (Dog) a;
            System.out.println("Downcast succeeded");
        } catch (ClassCastException e) {
            System.out.println("Downcast failed");
        }
    }
}
```
